MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_001: Phew... That was tough. It always is.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_002: Promised One, what are you doing here? Hope you\naren't coming to check on me.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_003: 'Cause you know I'm fine. This mercenary's seen\nmore than a few brutal battles in her day.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_004: But this last one...has me thinking of where I came\nfrom. I mean, originally.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_005: <NCA>"Where was that?"
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_006: I was born far away—out on the ocean, on one of\nthe farthest islands of Brigid.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_007: Peaceful place, even if we didn't have much.\nNo wars, no fights. Just...living.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_008: Nice for a kid. But it felt so darn small as I grew up.\nUntil the place got...stifling.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_009: Then one day, I up and left. Off to Dagda for a big\nlife of adventure, feasting, and fun.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_010: That is, I ran away from home—far as I could,\nacross the ocean.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_011: It wasn't easy, you know. I never could get settled in\none place, but the people I met became my family.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_012: I've had a full life, all things considered. I'm actually\npretty happy with the way it turned out.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_013: <NCA>"That's the most important thing."
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_014: Right. But, uh...now this war has spread across\nDagda. What future is there here, or anywhere?
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_015: Maybe I shouldn't have left home. Could've lived a\nlittle life in a little shack with my parents.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_016: Listen to me, the mighty Jasmine from the\nRains of Palma!
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_017: <NCA>"We need to fight for our future."
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_018: <NCB>"We'll fight onward, together."
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_019: <ACA>Yes, we will! We sure won't survive for long if we\nmope about the past.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_020: <ACB>Wow... It's an honor to get rallied by the\nPromised One. It means a lot.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_021: I really need to stop wasting my time with all this\nnonsense and just keep on moving!
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_022: <NCA>"But...take it easy now and then, OK?"
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_A_023: Heh. Take it easy? If you say so. It's not my strong\nsuit, but maybe I'll give it a try sometime.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_001: Look at that! Promised One, you survived. Though\nI always had a feeling you would.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_002: <NCA>"I'm glad to see that you survived too."
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_003: You and me both. I'm still not sure how I managed\nto stay in one piece.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_004: I don't even know what I'm going to do with myself\nnow, other than stay alive, I hope.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_005: I've been thinking about carrying on as a mercenary.\nIt's been a good life for me in a lot of ways.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_006: Then again, wasn't it you who told me I should "take\nit easy" every now and again?
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_007: I think I might follow your advice. For a while,\nat least.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_008: I've been battling on and on for so long that living\nany other way is going to feel strange.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_009: <NCA>"It's not strange at all to feel that way."
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_010: I appreciate that, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_011: To be honest, I've often had thoughts about hanging\nup my armor and settling down.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_012: Don't get me wrong, my husband put together the\ncrew and made a home for me in his own way.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_013: But the more I think about it, the more I want to\nreturn to my first home.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_014: So I'm going back to Brigid for a while. I don't know\nwhat comes after that. We'll just have to see.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_015: I'm going to invite the guys from my crew to come\nalong, if they want.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_016: Some of them are probably also wondering what's\nnext. I'm guessing they'll welcome the change.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_017: I'm worried though. When I left Brigid behind, I\nnever sent a letter back home. Not even one.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_018: Are my parents even alive? Do I have a home to\ngo back to? I...just don't know.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_019: If that is all back there, waiting for me, will—\nWill my parents forgive me? For just...leaving?
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_020: I guess I'll cross that bridge when I come to it.\nIt'll all work out, I'm sure!
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_021: <NCA>"I'm sure it will too."
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_022: <NCB>"You've made a good choice."
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_023: Haha. Well, if it's got your stamp of approval,\nPromised One, my future will be fiiine!
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_024: <RSDS>Now, I expect you to come visit me in Brigid, alright?\nYou know, if you have a spare moment.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_025: Even the Promised One needs to take it easy\nsometimes.
MID_SE_Ism_Jas_S_026: I swear, you will always have a hearty welcome\nfrom me. So, try to come visit, OK?